<section #l1-name | `<name>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `metadata` · Layer 1 `<name>` · JATS `<string-name>` · `content` `prose` → `<children>`

*No kwargs or boolean flags.*

Produced by: canonical `<name>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code #code:l1-name-1>
<author>
  <name | Jane Goodall>
</author>
</code>

*Structural / front-matter — shown as source. It carries metadata or apparatus (configuration, stored data, document front matter), not standalone body content, so there is no in-flow live box.*

*The common case. Pipe content becomes the name string.*

<code #code:l1-name-2>
<author name="Jane Goodall" orcid="0000-0001-2345-6789" +corresponding>
</code>

*Structural / front-matter — shown as source. It carries metadata or apparatus (configuration, stored data, document front matter), not standalone body content, so there is no in-flow live box.*

*Kwarg form of &lt;author&gt;. The `name` kwarg lifts to a &lt;name&gt; child tag at the normalize-to-canonical gate, parallel to &lt;meta&gt;'s kwarg-to-child-tag lift. The `+corresponding` boolean stays as a kwarg/attribute on the canonical Layer 1 &lt;author&gt; (it is a scalar marker, not a structured field).*

</section>

<section #l1-affiliation | `<affiliation>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `metadata` · Layer 1 `<affiliation>` · JATS `<aff>` · `content` `prose` → `<children>`

*No kwargs or boolean flags.*

Produced by: canonical `<affiliation>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code #code:l1-affiliation-1>
<author>
  <name | Jane Goodall>
  <affiliation | Anthropic>
</author>
</code>

*Structural / front-matter — shown as source. It carries metadata or apparatus (configuration, stored data, document front matter), not standalone body content, so there is no in-flow live box.*

*Simple author affiliation. The affiliation sits as a sub-element of &lt;author&gt;, parallel to other rich-author-metadata elements (&lt;orcid&gt;, &lt;email&gt;).*

<code #code:l1-affiliation-2>
<author>
  <name | Jane Goodall>
  <affiliation #aff1 | Anthropic, San Francisco, USA>
</author>
<author>
  <name | David Attenborough>
  <affiliation #aff1 />
</author>
</code>

*Structural / front-matter — shown as source. It carries metadata or apparatus (configuration, stored data, document front matter), not standalone body content, so there is no in-flow live box.*

*Shared affiliation. The id on the first affiliation lets subsequent authors reference the same one by id via a self-closing tag. JATS exporter generates the appropriate &lt;xref ref-type="aff" rid="aff1"&gt; structure.*

</section>

