<section #l1-date | `<date>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `metadata` · Layer 1 `<date>` · JATS `<pub-date or date (in history)>` · `content` `prose` → `<children>`

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `type` | kwarg | `publication` `submission` `acceptance` `revision` `retraction` `embargo` `other` | Distinguishes different kinds of dates. The default (publication) is the date the document was published. |
| `format` | kwarg | `iso` `ymd` `ymd-time` `mdy` `dmy` `custom` | Optional hint about how the date should be parsed and formatted. Default is iso (YYYY-MM-DD). |

Produced by: canonical `<date>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code #code:l1-date-1>
<date | 2024-03-15>
</code>

*Structural / front-matter — shown as source. It carries metadata or apparatus (configuration, stored data, document front matter), not standalone body content, so there is no in-flow live box.*

*Simple publication date. The type defaults to "publication" when not specified.*

<code #code:l1-date-2>
<date type=submission | 2023-11-01>
</code>

*Structural / front-matter — shown as source. It carries metadata or apparatus (configuration, stored data, document front matter), not standalone body content, so there is no in-flow live box.*

<code #code:l1-date-3>
<meta>
  <date type=submission | 2023-11-01>
  <date type=acceptance | 2024-02-10>
  <date type=publication | 2024-03-15>
</meta>
</code>

*Structural / front-matter — shown as source. It carries metadata or apparatus (configuration, stored data, document front matter), not standalone body content, so there is no in-flow live box.*

*Multiple dates of different types. The publication date is the primary; submission, acceptance, etc., go in JATS history.*

<code #code:l1-date-4>
<date | March 15, 2024>
</code>

*Structural / front-matter — shown as source. It carries metadata or apparatus (configuration, stored data, document front matter), not standalone body content, so there is no in-flow live box.*

*Free-form date format. Acceptable but ISO 8601 is preferred for machine readability and for predictable JATS export.*

</section>

<section #l1-publication-date | `<publication-date>`>

<sub-section | Specification>

`category` `metadata` · Layer 1 `<publication-date>` · JATS `<pub-date>` · `content` `prose` → `<children>`

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `format` | kwarg | `iso` `ymd` `ymd-time` `mdy` `dmy` `custom` | Optional hint about how the date should be parsed and formatted. Default is iso (YYYY-MM-DD). Same set as <date>'s format kwarg. |

Produced by: canonical `<publication-date>`.

<sub-section | Examples>

<code #code:l1-publication-date-1>
<meta>
  <publication-date | 2024-03-15>
</meta>
